# II. CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT CONCEPT

## *The Epistemic Liberty Amendment*

*(Draft language intentionally spare—constitutional text must breathe.)*

### Section 1

The right of the people to informed consent in matters materially affecting their bodily autonomy, liberty, property, or civic participation shall not be infringed by deception or concealment.

### Section 2

No law, policy, or institution may derive authority from consent obtained through the distortion or withholding of material information.

### Section 3

The people retain the right to access information necessary to assess risk, verify claims of authority, and withdraw from systems of governance or belief without concealed penalty.

### Section 4

Congress shall have power to enforce this article by appropriate legislation.

---

### Why This Works

* It doesn’t ban secrecy.
* It bans **illegitimate authority**.
* It ties power directly to epistemic honesty.

This amendment doesn’t weaken the state.
It removes its anesthesia.

